From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 10:06:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/30] jsonrpc: optional width/height/duration on MessageData
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Core measures images itself at send time (`try_calc_and_set_dimensions`), but it
has no audio or video decoder and never will — on wasm it runs in a Web Worker
with no DOM. So `Param::Duration` currently has exactly two sources: the
`Chat-Duration` header of an incoming message, and `dc_msg_set_duration`, which
only the mobile UIs call. Nothing on the jsonrpc API sets it.

The consequence is silent: `mimefactory` only writes `Chat-Duration` when the
param is > 0, so every voice message sent from desktop or the web app goes out
without one, and `PostMsgMetadata` carries `duration: None`, which is what the
receiver's download-on-demand placeholder has to render before the attachment
exists. Same for a video's pixel size, which no code path derives at all.

`MessageData` is the right place: the desktop composer does not send its draft,
it builds a fresh `MessageData` from the draft state and calls `send_msg`, so
params written onto the draft never reach the wire.

Passthrough only — `set_dimension`/`set_duration` are the same setters the C API
has always exposed, and the receiving side already rejects implausible durations
in `mimeparser`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 deltachat-jsonrpc/src/api/types/message.rs | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/deltachat-jsonrpc/src/api/types/message.rs b/deltachat-jsonrpc/src/api/types/message.rs
index 8884765..92b75f6 100644
--- a/deltachat-jsonrpc/src/api/types/message.rs
+++ b/deltachat-jsonrpc/src/api/types/message.rs
@@ -623,6 +623,20 @@ pub struct MessageData {
     /// Quoted message id. Takes preference over `quoted_text` (see below).
     pub quoted_message_id: Option<u32>,
     pub quoted_text: Option<String>,
+    /// Pixel size of an image or video attachment.
+    ///
+    /// Optional, and only needed for video: core measures images itself when the message is
+    /// sent, but it has no video decoder, so a UI that has one should pass the size here.
+    /// Both must be given for either to be used.
+    pub width: Option<i32>,
+    /// See [`MessageData::width`].
+    pub height: Option<i32>,
+    /// Duration of an audio, voice or video attachment, in milliseconds.
+    ///
+    /// Optional, and never derived by core, which cannot decode media. Passing it is what
+    /// makes the message carry a `Chat-Duration` header, which is what lets receivers show
+    /// the length before downloading the attachment.
+    pub duration: Option<i32>,
 }
 
 impl MessageData {
@@ -652,6 +666,12 @@ pub(crate) async fn create_message(self, context: &Context) -> Result<Message> {
         if let Some((latitude, longitude)) = self.location {
             message.set_location(latitude, longitude);
         }
+        if let (Some(width), Some(height)) = (self.width, self.height) {
+            message.set_dimension(width, height);
+        }
+        if let Some(duration) = self.duration {
+            message.set_duration(duration);
+        }
         if let Some(id) = self.quoted_message_id {
             let quoted_message = Message::load_from_db(context, MsgId::new(id))
                 .await
